WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.623
A provider deposited one ether and 2,000 dollars.

2
00:00:03.623 --> 00:00:09.033
The ether price doubled, and arbitrageurs bought the cheap ether out of the pool.

3
00:00:09.033 --> 00:00:14.376
Now the provider has 5,657 dollars, while simply holding would have given 6,000.

4
00:00:14.376 --> 00:00:18.985
The pool keeps selling what gets dearer and buying what gets cheaper.

5
00:00:18.985 --> 00:00:23.126
The loss is the same for a rise and a fall by the same factor.

6
00:00:24.126 --> 00:00:26.555
A provider earns fees from every swap,

7
00:00:26.555 --> 00:00:29.496
and the result is fees minus impermanent loss.

8
00:00:29.496 --> 00:00:32.372
For two dollar stablecoins the loss is small.

9
00:00:32.372 --> 00:00:36.592
If one coin can crash against the other, the loss eats everything.

10
00:00:36.592 --> 00:00:41.578
And liquidity in a narrow range earns more fees, but when the price leaves it,

11
00:00:41.578 --> 00:00:44.838
you are left entirely in the coin that got cheaper.
